============================================================================================
  EFFECT ON THE TIMESCALE CRITERION
============================================================================================
    tau_diff: 1017 s (Richardson) vs 987 s (datasheet), -2.91 %
    The criterion is eps = 7.48 (t/tau)^-1.18. A -2.91 %
    shift in tau moves every plotted ratio by the same factor, so the
    FITTED EXPONENT IS UNCHANGED and the crossings move by that amount:
        2.0 % error at t/tau = 3.49 -> 3.59 under the datasheet value
        5.0 % error at t/tau = 1.37 -> 1.41 under the datasheet value
       10.0 % error at t/tau = 0.77 -> 0.79 under the datasheet value
       25.0 % error at t/tau = 0.37 -> 0.38 under the datasheet value

